      "text": "A number is divisible by 18 if and only if it is divisible by both 9 and 2. Since the units digit of the number is $n$, we can conclude that the number is divisible by 2 if and only if $n$ is even.\n\nFor the number to be divisible by 9, the sum of its digits must be divisible by 9. Thus, we obtain that:\n\n\\[7+1+2+n \\equiv 0 \\pmod{9}\\implies n \\equiv 5 \\pmod{9}\\implies n=\\boxed{5}\\] We have the equation $712n+9n\\equiv 0\\mod{18}$. Dividing by $n$ (since it is not zero) $ \\implies 721\\equiv 0 \\mod{18}$. Since $721\\equiv 5 \\mod{18}$ (remember, we can just substitute $n$ with $5$), the answer is $5$.",
