      "text": "The number 712n is divisible by 18 if and only if it is divisible by both 9 and 2.\nFor divisibility by 2, the units digit must be even.\nTo have a units digit of $n$, $n$ must be one of the numbers $\\boxed{0, 2, 4, 6, \\text{ and } 8}$. To have digits sum to a multiple of 9, the digits $7, 1,$ and $2$ should have $n$ added to make a multiple of 9. Combining these two restrictions, it follows that the four-digit numbers divisible by 18 are $7120, 7122, 7124, 7126,$ and $7128$.\nAmong these, only $\\boxed{7128}$ is divisible by both 9 and 2. The answer is: 7128",
